<title>UK: TABLE-Portsmouth&amp;Sunderland yr profits rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Portsmouth&amp;Sunderland yr profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 29, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) (adjusted)  51.9		  vs  48.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   1.61		 vs   n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  14.48		 vs  12.87</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excepts	 9.3		  vs   9.0</p>
<p> Op profit (pre-excepts)  9.4		  vs   8.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   151.0		  vs 133.0</p>
<p>NOTE - After interest and exceptional costs, pretax profit was 7.5 million stg in 1996/97, while 1995/96's 18.6 million profit included the non-operating exceptional profit of 9.9 million on the sale of the Croydon Advertiser Group.</p>
<p>&quot;In line with its declared strategy, the group has completed an important stage in its development after two years of heavy investment, and now expects to see the benefit in increased profits, &quot; chairman Sir Richard Storey said in the results statement. &quot;The board remains confident of the prospects for both local publishing and local retailing and will continue to develop both&quot;.</p>
<p>Full company name - Portsmouth &amp; Sunderland Newspapers Plc .</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
